Beam cryptography (vendored)
----------------------------
The ECC and Bulletproof implementation under src/beam/core and the supporting
headers under src/beam/utility are from BeamMW/beam, revision
90a8be3ba2bed3e3adac748867658e9381b3f462 (Apache License 2.0).
See src/beam/LICENSE and the source copyright notices. HexWallet changed
include paths, entropy and error handling, lazy generator initialization,
precomputation table size, temporary storage and TLS access for the MCU.
The secp256k1 headers are from the Beam-pinned BeamMW/secp256k1 submodule,
revision 3ac4050e7bf914c59677c22aa4b9dba95cc40944 (MIT).
See src/beam/secp256k1/COPYING.

External libraries (not vendored)
---------------------------------
LVGL 9.5.0 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 LVGL Kft) is linked into display builds.
Mbed TLS 3.6.5 is dual-licensed Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later; this project
relies on the Apache-2.0 option. It comes from the ESP32 Arduino core on device
and from a pinned checkout in CI.
nayuki/QR-Code-generator (MIT) is a test-only oracle for
tests/host/qr_cross_check.cpp and is never linked into firmware.
NXP plug-and-trust is checked out at a pinned commit for the SE051 transport
compile check; no NXP source is redistributed here.
NXP SE051 APDU constants were cross-checked against the public generated APDU
layer in that repository; the applet specification itself is not public.

GxEPD2 (T-Deck Max only) - licensing conflict, read before distributing
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Board 4 (HEXWALLET_BOARD_T_DECK_MAX) compiles against GxEPD2 by Jean-Marc
Zingg, which is licensed GPL-3.0. GxEPD2 is not vendored; it is an external
Arduino library. A firmware image that links it is a combined work and must
satisfy GPL-3.0 for that combination, which is incompatible with the
non-commercial terms of LICENSE. Do not distribute a board-4 image until this is
resolved: either replace the backend with an in-tree driver or obtain compatible
terms from the GxEPD2 author. The ESP32-P4 e-paper path uses the in-tree SSD1680
driver (EinkPanel.cpp) and does not link GxEPD2.
XELIS native accounts
---------------------
The English and Simplified Chinese recovery dictionaries come from
xelis-project/xelis-blockchain, revision db59b5c246ab0e40386d6c241dcd77f0aea84b10.
The upstream BSD-3-Clause license is in src/xelis/LICENSE.
The portable Ristretto255 field and scalar code is from jedisct1/libsodium
1.0.20-RELEASE, revision 9511c982fb1d046470a8b42aa36556cdb7da15de.
The field implementation uses the upstream 10-limb configuration. Local
changes select that configuration and adjust includes for Arduino's build.
The upstream license is in src/xelis/ref10/LICENSE.
